# Everything here is excluded from the build context sent to the Docker daemon.
#
# This file did not exist, which meant every `docker compose build` uploaded the entire repository —
# node_modules, the Android build tree, the desktop AppImage output, backups. It also meant a single
# unreadable file anywhere in the tree failed the build outright: SwiftPM's .build directory is
# written by a root container (see docs/ios-build.md), so after any iOS build the next deploy died
# with "error from sender: open .../ModuleCache: permission denied" — a Swift artifact breaking the
# backend image.

# ---- dependencies (reinstalled inside the image from the lockfile) ----
node_modules
**/node_modules

# ---- build output ----
dist
**/dist
dist-owner
**/dist-owner
.next
**/.next

# ---- native toolchain output ----
# SwiftPM writes this as root from a container; it is also hundreds of megabytes.
apps/ios/**/.build
apps/android
apps/desktop/release
apps/mobile/android
apps/mobile/ios

# ---- local state that must never reach an image ----
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
secrets
backups
data/ipintel
downloads

# ---- version control and editor noise ----
.git
.gitignore
**/*.log
_tmp_*
.DS_Store
